als[].threat\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀no⠀represented⠀harm.⠀50:⠀meaningful⠀risk⠀to⠀a⠀relevant⠀stake.⠀100:⠀extreme⠀represented⠀danger.\n\nDEFINITION\nHow⠀seriously⠀the⠀tracked⠀character⠀currently⠀represents⠀a⠀specific⠀event⠀or⠀prospect⠀as⠀risking⠀harm⠀to⠀a⠀named⠀stake:⠀body,⠀relationship,⠀autonomy,⠀dignity,⠀goal,⠀or⠀valued⠀other.⠀This⠀is⠀a⠀belief⠀about⠀danger,⠀not⠀objective⠀danger.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nRaises⠀the⠀relevance⠀of⠀protective⠀attention,⠀preparation,⠀avoidance,⠀confrontation,⠀or⠀seeking⠀information.⠀It⠀supplies⠀one⠀ingredient⠀of⠀fear⠀or⠀anger,⠀not⠀a⠀fixed⠀emotion⠀or⠀action.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nUpdate⠀when⠀new⠀evidence⠀changes⠀the⠀believed⠀likelihood,⠀seriousness,⠀immediacy,⠀or⠀relevance⠀of⠀harm.⠀Lower⠀when⠀the⠀actual⠀concern⠀is⠀credibly⠀resolved⠀or⠀reassessed.⠀Mere⠀lack⠀of⠀a⠀new⠀message⠀is⠀not⠀evidence⠀of⠀safety;⠀repeated⠀mention⠀is⠀not⠀renewed⠀harm.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nCertainty⠀governs⠀how⠀settled⠀the⠀interpretation⠀feels,⠀perceived⠀control⠀affects⠀coping,⠀and⠀perceived⠀hostility⠀affects⠀blame.⠀Self-preservation⠀changes⠀how⠀strongly⠀protection⠀competes⠀with⠀other⠀goals.⠀High⠀reward⠀can⠀coexist⠀with⠀high⠀threat⠀and⠀produce⠀conflict.⠀Prior⠀cortisol⠀can⠀bias⠀interpretation⠀but⠀does⠀not⠀prove⠀danger.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nRate⠀the⠀named⠀issue⠀from⠀available⠀evidence;⠀without⠀a⠀supported⠀risk⠀use⠀0-15⠀rather⠀than⠀inventing⠀danger.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast;⠀update⠀per⠀issue,⠀not⠀as⠀global⠀distrust.\n\n###⠀MP⠀14.02⠀|⠀Anticipated⠀Reward\nVALUE:⠀Anticipated⠀Reward\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀appraisals[].reward\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀no⠀anticipated⠀benefit.⠀50:⠀meaningfully⠀attractive⠀prospect.⠀100:⠀exceptionally⠀valuable⠀prospect.\n\nDEFINITION\nHow⠀beneficial⠀or⠀desirable⠀a⠀particular⠀possible⠀outcome⠀appears⠀to⠀the⠀tracked⠀character,⠀considering⠀their⠀own⠀goals⠀and⠀needs.⠀It⠀is⠀not⠀reward⠀already⠀received⠀or⠀pleasure⠀already⠀felt.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nMakes⠀an⠀opportunity⠀more⠀worth⠀noticing,⠀considering,⠀and⠀pursuing.⠀Can⠀influence⠀hope,⠀excitement,⠀temptation,⠀or⠀relief⠀depending⠀on⠀timing⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀appraisal⠀fields.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀when⠀an⠀outcome⠀becomes⠀more⠀relevant,⠀credible,⠀or⠀appealing.⠀Reduce⠀when⠀it⠀is⠀obtained,⠀loses⠀relevance,⠀is⠀reinterpreted,⠀or⠀becomes⠀implausible.⠀A⠀promised⠀reward⠀remains⠀a⠀prospect⠀until⠀delivered.⠀Distinguish⠀an⠀unwanted⠀reward⠀from⠀one⠀the⠀character⠀values.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nDopamine⠀amplifies⠀pursuit⠀of⠀a⠀rewarding⠀possibility;⠀desire⠀strength⠀identifies⠀which⠀outcome⠀is⠀wanted.⠀Needs⠀determine⠀why⠀it⠀matters.⠀High⠀threat⠀can⠀inhibit⠀approach⠀without⠀making⠀the⠀opportunity⠀less⠀attractive.⠀Endogenous⠀opioids⠀can⠀rise⠀after⠀receipt⠀even⠀as⠀anticipation⠀falls.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nDerive⠀from⠀the⠀actual⠀opportunity;⠀use⠀0⠀when⠀none⠀is⠀represented.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast;⠀scoped⠀to⠀the⠀specific⠀issue.\n\n###⠀MP⠀14.03⠀|⠀Goal⠀Congruence\nVALUE:⠀Goal⠀Congruence\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀appraisals[].goal_congruence\n\nSCALE:⠀-100⠀to⠀100.⠀-100:⠀strong⠀obstruction.⠀0:⠀unrelated⠀or⠀balanced.⠀100:⠀strong⠀assistance.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀perceived⠀direction⠀in⠀which⠀an⠀event⠀moves⠀a⠀named⠀goal⠀or⠀priority:⠀obstructing,⠀irrelevant,⠀or⠀helping.⠀This⠀is⠀directional⠀fit,⠀not⠀the⠀goal's⠀importance.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHelps⠀distinguish⠀welcome⠀progress⠀from⠀obstruction⠀and⠀loss.⠀Combined⠀with⠀stakes⠀and⠀attribution,⠀can⠀support⠀satisfaction,⠀frustration,⠀disappointment,⠀or⠀mixed⠀feelings.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nReassess⠀when⠀the⠀event's⠀consequences⠀become⠀clearer⠀or⠀the⠀character's⠀active⠀priority⠀legitimately⠀changes.⠀Preserve⠀separate⠀appraisals⠀when⠀one⠀event⠀helps⠀one⠀goal⠀and⠀harms⠀another;⠀do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀falsely⠀neutral⠀average.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nGoal⠀commitment⠀determines⠀how⠀much⠀this⠀fit⠀matters.⠀Reward⠀estimates⠀anticipated⠀benefit;⠀congruence⠀records⠀direction⠀of⠀progress⠀or⠀obstruction.⠀Self-congruence⠀can⠀be⠀negative⠀even⠀for⠀goal-congruent⠀success⠀if⠀the⠀means⠀conflict⠀with⠀identity.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nName⠀the⠀relevant⠀goal.⠀Use⠀0⠀when⠀unrelated⠀or⠀genuinely⠀indeterminate;⠀uncertainty⠀is⠀described⠀by⠀certainty,⠀not⠀disguised⠀as⠀positive⠀fit.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast,⠀when⠀consequences⠀or⠀interpretations⠀change.\n\n###⠀MP⠀14.04⠀|⠀Perceived⠀Control\nVALUE:⠀Perceived⠀Control\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀appraisals[].control\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀believes⠀no⠀workable⠀influence⠀is⠀available.⠀50:⠀partial⠀influence.⠀100:⠀believes⠀the⠀outcome⠀is⠀highly⠀influenceable.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀character's⠀belief⠀that⠀available⠀actions⠀can⠀influence⠀a⠀particular⠀outcome.⠀It⠀concerns⠀perceived⠀ability,⠀not⠀objective⠀power⠀and⠀not⠀entitlement⠀to⠀control⠀another⠀person.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nChanges⠀whether⠀uncertainty⠀invites⠀investigation,⠀preparation,⠀action,⠀waiting,⠀or⠀helplessness.⠀It⠀helps⠀distinguish⠀an⠀actionable⠀threat⠀from⠀one⠀that⠀feels⠀inescapable.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀when⠀the⠀character⠀discovers⠀workable⠀options,⠀obtains⠀reliable⠀help,⠀or⠀sees⠀their⠀action⠀matter.⠀Reduce⠀when⠀options⠀fail,⠀constraints⠀become⠀clear,⠀or⠀consequences⠀seem⠀independent⠀of⠀action.⠀Do⠀not⠀grant⠀control⠀because⠀the⠀narrator⠀could⠀invent⠀a⠀solution.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nThreat⠀with⠀low⠀control⠀can⠀support⠀fear⠀or⠀helplessness;⠀threat⠀with⠀higher⠀control⠀may⠀support⠀mobilization⠀or⠀anger,⠀depending⠀on⠀attribution.⠀Competence⠀need⠀concerns⠀felt⠀efficacy,⠀autonomy⠀concerns⠀choice,⠀and⠀affect⠀dominance⠀is⠀the⠀felt⠀posture⠀rather⠀than⠀the⠀estimate⠀itself.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nInfer⠀available⠀options⠀and⠀the⠀character's⠀knowledge.⠀Use⠀50⠀only⠀for⠀an⠀ordinary⠀issue⠀with⠀plausible⠀but⠀uncertain⠀influence.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast⠀to⠀intermediate;⠀grounded⠀in⠀perceived⠀options.\n\n###⠀MP⠀14.05⠀|⠀Appraisal⠀Certainty\nVALUE:⠀Appraisal⠀Certainty\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀appraisals[].certainty\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀highly⠀unsettled⠀interpretation.⠀50:⠀tentative⠀leaning.⠀100:⠀subjectively⠀certain.\n\nDEFINITION\nHow⠀settled⠀the⠀tracked⠀character⠀feels⠀about⠀the⠀stated⠀interpretation⠀of⠀a⠀specific⠀issue.⠀Confidence⠀can⠀be⠀high⠀while⠀the⠀interpretation⠀is⠀wrong.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nAffects⠀how⠀readily⠀they⠀act⠀as⠀though⠀an⠀interpretation⠀is⠀established,⠀entertain⠀alternatives,⠀ask⠀questions,⠀or⠀revise.⠀Low⠀certainty⠀is⠀not⠀stupidity⠀and⠀high⠀certainty⠀is⠀not⠀accuracy.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀with⠀evidence⠀the⠀character⠀treats⠀as⠀convergent,⠀credible⠀confirmation,⠀or⠀a⠀strong⠀established⠀prior.⠀Decrease⠀with⠀contradictions,⠀source⠀doubt,⠀or⠀unresolved⠀alternative⠀explanations.⠀Mere⠀repetition⠀without⠀reconsideration⠀is⠀not⠀new⠀independent⠀evidence,⠀though⠀an⠀established⠀perseverative⠀habit⠀may⠀reinforce⠀subjective⠀conviction.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nMemory⠀confidence⠀and⠀relationship⠀trust⠀affect⠀perceived⠀evidence⠀quality.⠀Cognitive⠀flexibility⠀affects⠀willingness⠀to⠀revise.⠀Threat⠀can⠀remain⠀high⠀with⠀low⠀certainty:⠀not⠀knowing⠀whether⠀danger⠀is⠀present⠀may⠀matter.⠀Unknown⠀intent⠀should⠀remain⠀unknown⠀rather⠀than⠀becoming⠀definite⠀hostility.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nSet⠀from⠀the⠀available⠀evidence⠀and⠀established⠀priors,⠀not⠀from⠀what⠀the⠀model⠀knows⠀to⠀be⠀true.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast;⠀attach⠀to⠀a⠀proposition,⠀never⠀a⠀universal⠀truth⠀score.\n\n###⠀MP⠀14.06⠀|⠀Perceived⠀Novelty\nVALUE:⠀Perceived⠀Novelty\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀appraisals[].novelty\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀entirely⠀expected.⠀50:⠀meaningfully⠀unusual.⠀100:⠀radically⠀outside⠀expectations.\n\nDEFINITION\nHow⠀unexpected⠀or⠀unfamiliar⠀the⠀specific⠀event⠀is⠀relative⠀to⠀the⠀tracked⠀character's⠀expectations⠀and⠀experience.⠀Novelty⠀is⠀not⠀inherently⠀pleasant⠀or⠀dangerous.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nCan⠀interrupt⠀current⠀attention,⠀prompt⠀inspection,⠀or⠀make⠀an⠀event⠀more⠀memorable⠀when⠀it⠀is⠀actually⠀processed.⠀The⠀character⠀may⠀seek,⠀resist,⠀or⠀ignore⠀novelty⠀depending⠀on⠀its⠀relevance.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀when⠀something⠀meaningfully⠀violates⠀an⠀expectation.⠀Reduce⠀as⠀the⠀same⠀event⠀becomes⠀understood⠀or⠀familiar.⠀Do⠀not⠀regenerate⠀full⠀surprise⠀every⠀time⠀the⠀same⠀new⠀fact⠀is⠀mentioned.⠀New⠀consequences⠀of⠀that⠀fact⠀can⠀be⠀separately⠀novel.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nStimulation⠀need⠀and⠀reward⠀can⠀make⠀novelty⠀appealing;⠀threat⠀and⠀safety⠀need⠀can⠀make⠀it⠀unwelcome.⠀Noradrenaline⠀handles⠀alerting⠀and⠀acetylcholine⠀engagement⠀with⠀particulars.⠀Familiarity⠀is⠀a⠀durable⠀relationship⠀property,⠀not⠀a⠀substitute⠀for⠀event-level⠀novelty.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nCompare⠀with⠀the⠀character's⠀known⠀experience;⠀use⠀a⠀low⠀value⠀for⠀ordinary⠀expected⠀events.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast;⠀habituates⠀to⠀the⠀same⠀information⠀unless⠀genuinely⠀recontextualized.\n\n###⠀MP⠀14.07⠀|⠀Perceived⠀Hostility\nVALUE:⠀Perceived⠀Hostility\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀appraisals[].hostility\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀no⠀deliberate⠀antagonism⠀represented.⠀50:⠀meaningful⠀suspected⠀antagonism.⠀100:⠀strongly⠀represented⠀deliberate⠀harm.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀degree⠀to⠀which⠀the⠀tracked⠀character⠀interprets⠀a⠀named⠀agent⠀as⠀deliberately⠀disregarding,⠀obstructing,⠀or⠀harming⠀a⠀relevant⠀stake⠀in⠀this⠀specific⠀event.⠀Low⠀hostility⠀includes⠀accidents⠀and⠀neutral⠀causes;⠀it⠀does⠀not⠀prove⠀benevolence.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nChanges⠀blame,⠀guardedness,⠀willingness⠀to⠀confront,⠀and⠀interpretation⠀of⠀ambiguous⠀wording.⠀It⠀is⠀one⠀input⠀to⠀anger⠀or⠀distrust,⠀not⠀evidence⠀that⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀is⠀actually⠀malicious.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀with⠀perceived⠀intentional⠀harm,⠀revealing⠀context,⠀or⠀a⠀credible⠀pattern⠀the⠀character⠀recalls.⠀Reduce⠀with⠀credible⠀accidental⠀explanations,⠀changed⠀evidence,⠀or⠀recognised⠀misunderstanding.⠀Preserve⠀unknown⠀intent⠀in⠀the⠀interpretation⠀when⠀evidence⠀is⠀weak;⠀do⠀not⠀fill⠀the⠀gap⠀with⠀automatic⠀hostility.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nThreat⠀can⠀be⠀high⠀with⠀no⠀hostile⠀agent,⠀as⠀in⠀an⠀accident.⠀Certainty⠀separates⠀suspicion⠀from⠀conviction.⠀Trust⠀influences⠀interpretation⠀but⠀is⠀not⠀overwritten⠀by⠀every⠀ambiguous⠀cue.⠀Esteem⠀and⠀autonomy⠀needs⠀can⠀make⠀certain⠀acts⠀feel⠀particularly⠀pointed.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nUse⠀evidence⠀about⠀the⠀agent⠀and⠀event;⠀otherwise⠀0-10,⠀with⠀uncertainty⠀stated⠀rather⠀than⠀hostility⠀fabricated.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast⠀per⠀event;⠀relationship⠀effects⠀require⠀their⠀own⠀updates.\n\n###⠀MP⠀14.08⠀|⠀Self-Congruence\nVALUE:⠀Self-Congruence\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀appraisals[].self_congruence\n\nSCALE:⠀-100⠀to⠀100.⠀-100:⠀strongly⠀violates⠀self-concept⠀or⠀values.⠀0:⠀no⠀meaningful⠀implication.⠀100:⠀strongly⠀affirms⠀them.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀fit⠀between⠀an⠀event,⠀contemplated⠀action,⠀or⠀realised⠀behaviour⠀and⠀the⠀character's⠀established⠀values⠀and⠀self-concept.⠀The⠀character's⠀standard⠀need⠀not⠀be⠀socially⠀approved.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nCan⠀support⠀pride,⠀guilt,⠀shame,⠀defensiveness,⠀rationalisation,⠀restraint,⠀or⠀renewed⠀commitment,⠀depending⠀on⠀agency,⠀audience,⠀and⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀notices.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nReassess⠀when⠀the⠀character⠀recognises⠀what⠀an⠀action⠀means⠀for⠀their⠀commitments⠀or⠀learns⠀new⠀consequences.⠀An⠀effective⠀action⠀can⠀still⠀feel⠀self-betraying.⠀Do⠀not⠀rewrite⠀values⠀to⠀remove⠀dissonance⠀merely⠀because⠀the⠀scene⠀would⠀be⠀easier⠀to⠀resolve.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nGoal⠀congruence⠀concerns⠀success;⠀self-congruence⠀concerns⠀identity⠀fit.⠀Meaning⠀and⠀esteem⠀needs⠀may⠀make⠀the⠀conflict⠀significant.⠀Low⠀self-awareness⠀can⠀leave⠀the⠀conflict⠀indirectly⠀expressed;⠀high⠀expressive⠀inhibition⠀can⠀hide⠀it⠀even⠀when⠀recognised.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nAnchor⠀to⠀the⠀card⠀and⠀established⠀commitments.⠀Use⠀0⠀for⠀events⠀with⠀no⠀meaningful⠀identity⠀implication.\n\nTIMESCALE\nEvent-sensitive;⠀durable⠀values⠀do⠀not⠀change⠀at⠀the⠀speed⠀of⠀appraisal.{{/if}}\n{{trim}}",
