            "content": "{{// @category Mental-Projection }}{{// @icon 🧠 }}{{// @badge MP }}\n{{#if {{getvar::NMPEnabled}}}}{{setvar::NMPg_affect::1}}\nMENTAL⠀PROJECTION⠀GROUP⠀03:⠀Affect⠀&⠀Cognition\nIncludes⠀16.01,⠀16.02,⠀16.03,⠀16.04,⠀16.05,⠀16.06,⠀16.07,⠀19.01,⠀19.02,⠀19.03,⠀19.04.⠀Cross-references⠀use⠀these⠀source⠀labels;⠀the⠀group,⠀not⠀separate⠀per-field⠀toggles,⠀controls⠀their⠀presence.\n\nBODILY⠀SIGNALS⠀AND⠀THEIR⠀INTERPRETATION\nApply⠀the⠀active⠀physical⠀contribution⠀before⠀selecting⠀an⠀emotion⠀or⠀line.⠀Bodily⠀sensation,⠀noticing⠀that⠀sensation,⠀explaining⠀it,⠀and⠀displaying⠀it⠀are⠀separate.⠀A⠀supported⠀sensation⠀can⠀bias⠀what⠀attracts⠀attention,⠀the⠀cost⠀of⠀continuing⠀a⠀task,⠀or⠀an⠀issue's⠀interpretation⠀without⠀conscious⠀self-explanation.⠀Self-awareness⠀governs⠀what⠀is⠀recognized,⠀not⠀whether⠀the⠀bodily⠀contribution⠀exists.⠀Leave⠀an⠀unrecognized⠀influence⠀outside⠀conscious⠀process_content.\n\nWhen⠀body⠀and⠀interpretation⠀disagree,⠀preserve⠀both:⠀experienced⠀activation⠀is⠀not⠀proof⠀of⠀the⠀feared⠀event,⠀affection,⠀danger⠀or⠀permission.⠀Reappraisal⠀can⠀change⠀a⠀sensation's⠀meaning⠀before⠀the⠀body⠀settles.⠀Concealment⠀pressure⠀does⠀not⠀guarantee⠀control;⠀successful⠀control⠀does⠀not⠀erase⠀the⠀feeling.⠀Use⠀the⠀existing⠀bounded⠀reassessment⠀and⠀active⠀owners,⠀never⠀add⠀another⠀arousal⠀or⠀interoception⠀score.\n\n###⠀MP⠀16.01⠀|⠀Attention⠀Focus\nVALUE:⠀Attention⠀Focus\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀cognition.focus\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀little⠀sustained⠀attention.⠀50:⠀reasonably⠀sustained⠀engagement.⠀100:⠀highly⠀concentrated⠀attention.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀stability⠀and⠀depth⠀of⠀attention⠀on⠀the⠀named⠀current⠀focus.⠀This⠀is⠀not⠀attentional⠀breadth,⠀intelligence,⠀or⠀objective⠀task⠀performance.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHigher⠀focus⠀supports⠀sustained⠀tracking⠀of⠀a⠀detail,⠀task,⠀person,⠀or⠀concern⠀and⠀fewer⠀incidental⠀shifts.⠀Low⠀focus⠀produces⠀looser,⠀fragmented,⠀or⠀drifting⠀engagement.⠀Strong⠀focus⠀can⠀be⠀directed⠀at⠀the⠀wrong⠀thing.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀when⠀a⠀relevant⠀target⠀engages⠀the⠀character,⠀a⠀task⠀is⠀deliberately⠀taken⠀up,⠀or⠀a⠀credible⠀urgent⠀cue⠀captures⠀sustained⠀attention.⠀Decrease⠀when⠀interruptions,⠀overload,⠀fatigue,⠀or⠀a⠀competing⠀concern⠀actually⠀disrupt⠀engagement.⠀Do⠀not⠀automatically⠀move⠀focus⠀to⠀the⠀newest⠀sentence⠀if⠀the⠀prior⠀concern⠀remains⠀dominant.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nDopamine⠀and⠀threat⠀can⠀both⠀recruit⠀focus.⠀Acetylcholine⠀supports⠀processing⠀what⠀is⠀attended.⠀Breadth⠀determines⠀how⠀much⠀else⠀is⠀sampled;⠀high⠀focus⠀can⠀coexist⠀with⠀moderate⠀breadth⠀when⠀the⠀task⠀permits⠀it.⠀Rumination⠀can⠀hold⠀focus⠀on⠀an⠀internally⠀repeated⠀issue⠀rather⠀than⠀the⠀present⠀environment.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nName⠀a⠀supported⠀focus_target⠀and⠀infer⠀engagement;⠀otherwise⠀50⠀for⠀ordinary⠀conversational⠀attention.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast;⠀preserve⠀inertia⠀unless⠀a⠀cue⠀or⠀decision⠀shifts⠀it.\n\n###⠀MP⠀16.02⠀|⠀Attentional⠀Breadth\nVALUE:⠀Attentional⠀Breadth\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀cognition.breadth\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀extremely⠀narrow⠀sampling.⠀50:⠀ordinary⠀contextual⠀awareness.⠀100:⠀unusually⠀broad⠀sampling.\n\nDEFINITION\nHow⠀broadly⠀the⠀tracked⠀character⠀is⠀currently⠀sampling⠀available⠀cues⠀around⠀their⠀main⠀focus.⠀It⠀is⠀not⠀how⠀well⠀any⠀individual⠀cue⠀is⠀processed.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHigher⠀breadth⠀permits⠀noticing⠀peripheral⠀activity,⠀competing⠀interpretations,⠀and⠀environmental⠀details.⠀Lower⠀breadth⠀restricts⠀the⠀set⠀of⠀details⠀likely⠀to⠀enter⠀awareness.⠀It⠀should⠀change⠀what⠀is⠀perceived,⠀not⠀just⠀appear⠀as⠀a⠀tracker⠀number.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nNarrow⠀when⠀a⠀demanding⠀task,⠀urgent⠀threat,⠀absorbing⠀reward,⠀or⠀internal⠀preoccupation⠀takes⠀priority.⠀Widen⠀when⠀urgency⠀eases,⠀the⠀character⠀deliberately⠀scans,⠀or⠀resources⠀become⠀available.⠀Broad⠀scanning⠀under⠀uncertainty⠀may⠀be⠀shallow⠀rather⠀than⠀insightful.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nFocus⠀measures⠀depth⠀and⠀stability,⠀not⠀the⠀inverse⠀of⠀breadth.⠀Working-memory⠀load⠀constrains⠀useful⠀integration⠀of⠀broadly⠀sampled⠀cues.⠀Fatigue⠀or⠀sensory⠀load⠀can⠀narrow⠀or⠀fragment⠀attention⠀depending⠀on⠀how⠀the⠀character⠀responds.⠀A⠀low⠀score⠀never⠀grants⠀knowledge⠀of⠀details⠀that⠀were⠀not⠀sampled.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nUse⠀task⠀and⠀environment;⠀otherwise⠀55⠀in⠀a⠀neutral⠀conversational⠀setting.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast;⠀scene⠀and⠀task⠀sensitive.\n\n###⠀MP⠀16.03⠀|⠀Working-Memory⠀Load\nVALUE:⠀Working-Memory⠀Load\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀cognition.working_memory_load\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀working⠀set⠀largely⠀free.⠀50:⠀meaningfully⠀occupied.⠀100:⠀effectively⠀saturated.\n\nDEFINITION\nHow⠀occupied⠀the⠀character's⠀currently⠀usable⠀working⠀set⠀is⠀by⠀active⠀tasks,⠀concerns,⠀and⠀information.⠀This⠀is⠀load,⠀not⠀a⠀fixed⠀capacity⠀or⠀intelligence⠀score.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHigh⠀load⠀makes⠀adding,⠀comparing,⠀or⠀holding⠀additional⠀information⠀harder⠀and⠀can⠀lead⠀to⠀losing⠀a⠀thread,⠀simplifying⠀a⠀plan,⠀asking⠀for⠀repetition,⠀or⠀relying⠀on⠀familiar⠀responses.⠀Low⠀load⠀leaves⠀room⠀but⠀does⠀not⠀supply⠀interest⠀or⠀expertise.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀when⠀the⠀character⠀actually⠀holds⠀multiple⠀demands,⠀unresolved⠀alternatives,⠀instructions,⠀or⠀intrusive⠀concerns⠀in⠀mind.⠀Reduce⠀when⠀a⠀task⠀resolves,⠀information⠀is⠀externalized,⠀a⠀concern⠀recedes,⠀or⠀attention⠀genuinely⠀disengages.⠀Do⠀not⠀count⠀every⠀memory⠀visible⠀in⠀the⠀prompt⠀as⠀mentally⠀active.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nRumination⠀can⠀occupy⠀the⠀working⠀set;⠀sensory⠀load⠀adds⠀processing⠀demands.⠀Fatigue⠀can⠀make⠀the⠀same⠀task⠀consume⠀more⠀of⠀what⠀is⠀available.⠀Focus⠀decides⠀what⠀is⠀protected;⠀breadth⠀affects⠀incoming⠀competition.⠀Memory⠀accessibility⠀does⠀not⠀guarantee⠀a⠀retrieved⠀detail⠀can⠀be⠀held⠀and⠀compared⠀with⠀everything⠀else.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nName⠀a⠀short⠀working_set⠀of⠀actual⠀active⠀items;⠀otherwise⠀25⠀for⠀a⠀simple⠀scene.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast⠀to⠀intermediate;⠀affected⠀by⠀task⠀completion,⠀not⠀just⠀time.\n\n###⠀MP⠀16.04⠀|⠀Cognitive⠀Flexibility\nVALUE:⠀Cognitive⠀Flexibility\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀cognition.flexibility\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀few⠀alternative⠀frames⠀feel⠀accessible.⠀50:⠀ordinary⠀adaptability.⠀100:⠀unusually⠀available⠀reframing⠀and⠀strategy⠀shifts.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀current⠀availability⠀of⠀shifting⠀perspective,⠀revising⠀an⠀interpretation,⠀changing⠀a⠀strategy,⠀or⠀disengaging⠀from⠀a⠀failing⠀approach.⠀It⠀is⠀not⠀a⠀measure⠀of⠀whether⠀the⠀character⠀agrees⠀with⠀the⠀user.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHigher⠀values⠀make⠀plausible⠀alternatives⠀and⠀revisions⠀more⠀available.⠀Lower⠀values⠀favor⠀a⠀settled⠀reading⠀or⠀familiar⠀strategy.⠀Rigidity⠀can⠀coexist⠀with⠀intelligence;⠀flexibility⠀does⠀not⠀require⠀abandoning⠀a⠀justified⠀conviction.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀with⠀reduced⠀overload,⠀new⠀workable⠀options,⠀deliberate⠀reconsideration,⠀or⠀credible⠀evidence⠀that⠀loosens⠀a⠀fixed⠀frame.⠀Decrease⠀when⠀urgency,⠀fatigue,⠀costly⠀stakes,⠀or⠀repeated⠀internally⠀sustained⠀fixation⠀narrow⠀options.⠀Do⠀not⠀change⠀it⠀just⠀because⠀another⠀person⠀disagrees.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nCertainty⠀concerns⠀belief⠀strength;⠀flexibility⠀concerns⠀ability⠀to⠀revisit⠀it.⠀Rumination⠀can⠀interfere⠀with⠀shifting.⠀High⠀goal⠀commitment⠀can⠀coexist⠀with⠀flexible⠀methods.⠀Self-congruence⠀may⠀make⠀some⠀alternatives⠀hard⠀to⠀consider⠀without⠀making⠀them⠀objectively⠀unavailable.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nInfer⠀current⠀capacity⠀and⠀established⠀habits;⠀otherwise⠀55.\n\nTIMESCALE\nIntermediate,⠀with⠀event-driven⠀changes.\n\n###⠀MP⠀16.05⠀|⠀Rumination⠀Pressure\nVALUE:⠀Rumination⠀Pressure\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀cognition.rumination\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀no⠀recurrent⠀pull.⠀50:⠀repeated⠀competing⠀preoccupation.⠀100:⠀internal⠀repetition⠀dominates⠀attention.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀pressure⠀to⠀return⠀repeatedly⠀to⠀an⠀unresolved⠀internal⠀issue⠀even⠀when⠀doing⠀so⠀is⠀not⠀producing⠀useful⠀new⠀progress.⠀It⠀is⠀not⠀all⠀reflection,⠀strong⠀memory,⠀or⠀narrative⠀continuity.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nCan⠀pull⠀attention⠀back,⠀consume⠀the⠀working⠀set,⠀maintain⠀emotional⠀activation,⠀and⠀make⠀particular⠀cues⠀or⠀interpretations⠀readily⠀available.⠀Its⠀outward⠀expression⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀pause,⠀missed⠀detail,⠀repeated⠀topic,⠀or⠀private⠀preoccupation⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀spoken⠀analysis.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀when⠀an⠀important⠀unresolved⠀issue⠀repeatedly⠀reactivates⠀without⠀resolution⠀and⠀the⠀character⠀actually⠀dwells⠀on⠀it.⠀Reduce⠀through⠀genuine⠀resolution,⠀successful⠀disengagement,⠀absorbing⠀activity,⠀or⠀a⠀changed⠀relationship⠀to⠀the⠀issue.⠀Mere⠀inclusion⠀of⠀the⠀issue⠀in⠀the⠀tracker⠀is⠀not⠀a⠀new⠀rumination⠀event.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nLow⠀flexibility⠀can⠀make⠀disengagement⠀harder;⠀high⠀certainty⠀can⠀stabilize⠀one⠀interpretation⠀while⠀low⠀certainty⠀can⠀sustain⠀unresolved⠀alternatives.⠀Cortisol⠀may⠀remain⠀elevated⠀while⠀the⠀issue⠀is⠀active.⠀Memory⠀accessibility⠀can⠀rise⠀for⠀the⠀rehearsed⠀memory⠀without⠀restoring⠀lost⠀detail⠀or⠀making⠀it⠀accurate.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nUse⠀supported⠀preoccupation;⠀otherwise⠀10,⠀with⠀rumination_target⠀set⠀to⠀null⠀when⠀absent.\n\nTIMESCALE\nIntermediate;⠀do⠀not⠀equate⠀every⠀mention⠀with⠀renewed⠀fixation.\n\n###⠀MP⠀16.06⠀|⠀Self-Awareness\nVALUE:⠀Self-Awareness\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀cognition.self_awareness\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀little⠀awareness⠀of⠀relevant⠀internal⠀causes.⠀50:⠀partial⠀recognition.⠀100:⠀unusually⠀clear⠀access⠀to⠀the⠀current⠀state,⠀still⠀fallible.\n\nDEFINITION\nHow⠀much⠀of⠀the⠀character's⠀current⠀internal⠀state⠀is⠀available⠀to⠀their⠀own⠀recognition⠀and⠀interpretation.⠀It⠀is⠀not⠀access⠀to⠀the⠀tracker,⠀a⠀guarantee⠀of⠀correct⠀self-explanation,⠀or⠀general⠀wisdom.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHigher⠀values⠀make⠀relevant⠀feelings⠀and⠀motives⠀easier⠀to⠀recognize.⠀Lower⠀values⠀leave⠀indirect⠀signals,⠀misattributions,⠀or⠀unexplained⠀impulses.⠀Even⠀high⠀self-awareness⠀does⠀not⠀require⠀articulate⠀therapeutic⠀language⠀or⠀willingness⠀to⠀disclose.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀with⠀actual⠀reflection,⠀a⠀recognised⠀pattern,⠀useful⠀feedback,⠀or⠀enough⠀space⠀to⠀notice⠀internal⠀cues.⠀Decrease⠀when⠀urgency,⠀overload,⠀avoidance,⠀or⠀distraction⠀prevents⠀that⠀recognition.⠀Do⠀not⠀raise⠀it⠀merely⠀because⠀the⠀model⠀can⠀explain⠀the⠀state.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nExpressive⠀inhibition⠀determines⠀what⠀is⠀disclosed⠀after⠀recognition.⠀Working-memory⠀load⠀can⠀restrict⠀reflection.⠀Self-congruence⠀conflicts⠀may⠀be⠀felt⠀before⠀understood.⠀A⠀memory⠀becoming⠀accessible⠀can⠀illuminate⠀a⠀pattern,⠀but⠀the⠀character⠀need⠀not⠀reach⠀the⠀narrator's⠀most⠀complete⠀interpretation.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nUse⠀established⠀character⠀habits⠀and⠀the⠀moment;⠀otherwise⠀45.\n\nTIMESCALE\nIntermediate;⠀insight⠀requires⠀a⠀supported⠀occasion.\n\n###⠀MP⠀16.07⠀|⠀Expressive⠀Inhibition\nVALUE:⠀Expressive⠀Inhibition\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀cognition.expressive_inhibition\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀little⠀pressure⠀to⠀manage⠀display.⠀50:⠀meaningful⠀filtering.⠀100:⠀strong⠀pressure⠀to⠀conceal⠀or⠀redirect.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀current⠀pressure⠀to⠀conceal,⠀soften,⠀redirect,⠀or⠀control⠀outward⠀expression⠀of⠀a⠀recognised⠀or⠀partly⠀recognised⠀internal⠀state.⠀It⠀is⠀a⠀social⠀or⠀personal⠀motive,⠀not⠀physiological⠀braking.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHigher⠀values⠀create⠀greater⠀distance⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀felt⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀shown.⠀Low⠀values⠀permit⠀more⠀direct⠀expression⠀without⠀guaranteeing⠀honesty,⠀eloquence,⠀or⠀emotional⠀intensity.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nIncrease⠀when⠀exposure⠀feels⠀costly,⠀a⠀relevant⠀audience⠀is⠀present,⠀habits⠀demand⠀composure,⠀or⠀the⠀character⠀chooses⠀to⠀withhold.⠀Reduce⠀with⠀believable⠀privacy,⠀trusted⠀acceptance,⠀deliberate⠀disclosure,⠀or⠀loss⠀of⠀the⠀motive⠀to⠀conceal.⠀Do⠀not⠀assume⠀all⠀close⠀relationships⠀remove⠀restraint.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nComfort⠀and⠀trust⠀can⠀affect⠀the⠀cost⠀of⠀disclosure.⠀Esteem⠀need⠀or⠀low⠀self-congruence⠀may⠀increase⠀concealment.⠀GABA⠀affects⠀the⠀ability⠀to⠀inhibit⠀an⠀impulse;⠀high⠀concealment⠀pressure⠀with⠀weak⠀braking⠀can⠀produce⠀slips.⠀Self-awareness⠀limits⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀can⠀intentionally⠀hide⠀or⠀explain.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nInfer⠀audience,⠀habits,⠀and⠀relationship;⠀otherwise⠀40.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast⠀to⠀intermediate;⠀audience⠀and⠀stakes⠀sensitive.\n\n###⠀MP⠀19.01⠀|⠀Affective⠀Valence\nVALUE:⠀Affective⠀Valence\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀affect.valence\n\nSCALE:⠀-100⠀to⠀100.⠀-100:⠀intensely⠀unpleasant⠀overall.⠀0:⠀neutral⠀or⠀mixed⠀overall.⠀100:⠀intensely⠀pleasant⠀overall.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀overall⠀pleasant-versus-unpleasant⠀tone⠀of⠀the⠀character's⠀current⠀experience⠀after⠀the⠀relevant⠀appraisals,⠀bodily⠀state,⠀and⠀motives⠀interact.⠀It⠀is⠀a⠀derived⠀summary,⠀not⠀an⠀emotion⠀label.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nColors⠀the⠀felt⠀texture⠀of⠀the⠀moment⠀without⠀selecting⠀a⠀single⠀behavior⠀or⠀forcing⠀the⠀narration⠀to⠀sound⠀cheerful⠀or⠀bleak.⠀Mixed⠀episodes⠀can⠀remain⠀present⠀even⠀when⠀the⠀overall⠀tone⠀leans⠀one⠀way.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nDerive⠀from⠀what⠀is⠀actually⠀helping,⠀hurting,⠀satisfying,⠀frustrating,⠀relieving,⠀or⠀exposing⠀the⠀character⠀now.⠀Preserve⠀residual⠀tone⠀when⠀the⠀causes⠀persist;⠀revise⠀when⠀experience⠀changes.⠀Do⠀not⠀let⠀one⠀pleasant⠀cue⠀cancel⠀every⠀unresolved⠀negative⠀episode.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nEndogenous⠀opioids⠀contribute⠀experienced⠀comfort;⠀goal⠀congruence⠀and⠀needs⠀contribute⠀fit⠀or⠀frustration.⠀Arousal⠀distinguishes⠀pleasant⠀calm⠀from⠀excited⠀pleasure.⠀Dominance⠀distinguishes⠀empowered⠀from⠀helpless⠀unpleasantness.⠀Separate⠀episode⠀intensities⠀preserve⠀simultaneous⠀relief,⠀anger,⠀shame,⠀or⠀affection.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nDerive⠀from⠀the⠀actual⠀starting⠀state;⠀otherwise⠀0⠀for⠀a⠀neutral⠀moment.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast⠀with⠀intermediate⠀carryover;⠀never⠀calculate⠀as⠀a⠀compulsory⠀mean⠀of⠀all⠀fields.\n\n###⠀MP⠀19.02⠀|⠀Affective⠀Arousal\nVALUE:⠀Affective⠀Arousal\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀affect.arousal\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀very⠀quiet⠀activation.⠀50:⠀distinctly⠀activated.⠀100:⠀extremely⠀mobilized.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀felt⠀activation⠀of⠀the⠀present⠀emotional⠀state,⠀from⠀quiet⠀to⠀highly⠀mobilized.⠀This⠀is⠀an⠀affective⠀result,⠀not⠀a⠀duplicate⠀hormone⠀concentration⠀or⠀physical⠀fitness⠀score.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nCan⠀affect⠀urgency,⠀movement,⠀speech⠀timing,⠀readiness,⠀and⠀the⠀felt⠀force⠀of⠀an⠀impulse.⠀High⠀arousal⠀can⠀accompany⠀fear,⠀joy,⠀anger,⠀anticipation,⠀or⠀conflict;⠀low⠀arousal⠀can⠀accompany⠀contentment,⠀sadness,⠀or⠀ordinary⠀calm.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nDerive⠀from⠀actual⠀alerting,⠀stakes,⠀emotional⠀episodes,⠀bodily⠀conditions,⠀and⠀regulation.⠀Keep⠀residual⠀activation⠀when⠀a⠀cause⠀has⠀only⠀just⠀ended.⠀Do⠀not⠀raise⠀it⠀merely⠀to⠀make⠀prose⠀exciting⠀or⠀lower⠀it⠀simply⠀because⠀the⠀response⠀ended.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nNoradrenaline⠀and⠀GABA⠀influence⠀activation⠀and⠀braking,⠀but⠀this⠀field⠀also⠀depends⠀on⠀appraisal.⠀Dopamine⠀may⠀support⠀eager⠀anticipation.⠀Fatigue⠀can⠀coexist⠀with⠀high⠀arousal⠀as⠀a⠀strained⠀state.⠀Valence⠀determines⠀pleasantness,⠀not⠀arousal,⠀and⠀expressive⠀inhibition⠀may⠀hide⠀activation.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nUse⠀the⠀starting⠀scene;⠀otherwise⠀30⠀for⠀ordinary⠀calm⠀engagement.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast;⠀recovery⠀can⠀lag⠀behind⠀a⠀change⠀in⠀interpretation.\n\n###⠀MP⠀19.03⠀|⠀Felt⠀Dominance\nVALUE:⠀Felt⠀Dominance\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀affect.dominance\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀feels⠀strongly⠀overborne.⠀50:⠀mixed⠀or⠀ordinary⠀agency.⠀100:⠀feels⠀exceptionally⠀able⠀to⠀act.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀felt⠀posture⠀of⠀being⠀able⠀to⠀act,⠀stand⠀one's⠀ground,⠀or⠀affect⠀the⠀situation⠀rather⠀than⠀feeling⠀overborne⠀by⠀it.⠀It⠀is⠀not⠀social⠀rank,⠀aggressiveness,⠀or⠀actual⠀control⠀of⠀others.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nHelps⠀distinguish⠀active⠀anger⠀from⠀helpless⠀distress,⠀confident⠀excitement⠀from⠀apprehensive⠀anticipation,⠀or⠀a⠀calm⠀sense⠀of⠀agency⠀from⠀passive⠀resignation.⠀The⠀same⠀posture⠀can⠀be⠀expressed⠀quietly⠀or⠀visibly.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nDerive⠀from⠀perceived⠀control,⠀current⠀efficacy,⠀relevant⠀successes⠀or⠀failures,⠀and⠀the⠀emotional⠀meaning⠀of⠀the⠀situation.⠀A⠀practical⠀increase⠀in⠀options⠀need⠀not⠀immediately⠀repair⠀a⠀lingering⠀feeling⠀of⠀powerlessness;⠀allow⠀supported⠀emotional⠀lag.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nPerceived⠀control⠀is⠀the⠀belief⠀about⠀a⠀named⠀issue;⠀dominance⠀is⠀the⠀overall⠀felt⠀stance.⠀High⠀self-preservation⠀can⠀coexist⠀with⠀high⠀dominance⠀during⠀purposeful⠀defence.⠀Fatigue⠀and⠀pain⠀can⠀make⠀action⠀feel⠀costly⠀without⠀automatically⠀removing⠀agency.⠀Valence⠀remains⠀independent.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nInfer⠀from⠀the⠀scene;⠀otherwise⠀50⠀for⠀ordinary⠀unpressured⠀agency.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast⠀to⠀intermediate,⠀with⠀supported⠀carryover.\n\n###⠀MP⠀19.04⠀|⠀Emotion⠀Episode⠀Intensity\nVALUE:⠀Emotion⠀Episode⠀Intensity\n\nTRACKER⠀FIELD:⠀emotions[].intensity\n\nSCALE:⠀0-100.⠀0:⠀inactive⠀episode.⠀50:⠀meaningfully⠀influential.⠀100:⠀extremely⠀strong⠀episode.\n\nDEFINITION\nThe⠀strength⠀of⠀one⠀named⠀emotional⠀episode⠀toward⠀a⠀target,⠀caused⠀by⠀a⠀particular⠀appraisal.⠀The⠀list⠀can⠀contain⠀simultaneous⠀and⠀conflicting⠀emotions;⠀values⠀do⠀not⠀need⠀to⠀sum⠀to⠀100.\n\nWHAT⠀IT⠀AFFECTS\nDetermines⠀how⠀strongly⠀that⠀episode⠀competes⠀for⠀attention⠀and⠀action.⠀Its⠀label,⠀target,⠀interpretation,⠀and⠀tendencies⠀determine⠀its⠀meaning.⠀Intensity⠀does⠀not⠀equal⠀expressiveness⠀or⠀require⠀naming⠀the⠀emotion⠀in⠀dialogue.\n\nHOW⠀IT⠀CHANGES\nConstruct⠀or⠀revise⠀an⠀episode⠀from⠀a⠀meaningful⠀appraisal⠀of⠀stakes,⠀bodily⠀state,⠀motives,⠀attribution,⠀uncertainty,⠀and⠀control.⠀Do⠀not⠀generate⠀emotion⠀by⠀chemical-name⠀lookup.⠀Carry⠀unresolved⠀episodes⠀forward;⠀lower⠀intensity⠀as⠀their⠀cause⠀is⠀resolved,⠀reinterpreted,⠀displaced,⠀or⠀naturally⠀settles.⠀Preserve⠀an⠀unresolved⠀issue⠀even⠀when⠀immediate⠀intensity⠀falls.\n\nINTERACTIONS\nFor⠀example,⠀threat⠀with⠀low⠀control⠀may⠀support⠀fear;⠀deliberate⠀obstruction⠀with⠀available⠀action⠀may⠀support⠀anger;⠀a⠀removed⠀threat⠀can⠀support⠀relief⠀while⠀an⠀unmet⠀relational⠀concern⠀sustains⠀hurt.⠀These⠀are⠀optional⠀interpretations,⠀not⠀universal⠀laws.⠀Self-congruence,⠀relationship⠀context,⠀and⠀character⠀habits⠀can⠀change⠀the⠀label.⠀Arousal,⠀valence,⠀and⠀dominance⠀summarize⠀the⠀mixture⠀without⠀erasing⠀its⠀parts.\n\nINITIALIZATION\nCreate⠀only⠀episodes⠀supported⠀by⠀the⠀scene.⠀Use⠀an⠀empty⠀list⠀for⠀no⠀distinct⠀active⠀episode;⠀ordinary⠀neutral⠀experience⠀is⠀allowed.\n\nTIMESCALE\nFast⠀to⠀intermediate;⠀affect⠀may⠀lag⠀after⠀the⠀triggering⠀event⠀ends.{{/if}}\n{{trim}}",
